  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionId": "section-introduction",
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "sourceAnchor": "introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n\tThe Street Justice feat is a fantastic option for grapple enthusiasts,\n\tallowing you to support your allies, quickly bind enemies in chains, and\n\tgenerally make your enemies an easy target.\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n\tWhile Street Justice doesn’t require the Grappler feat, the two work very\n\tnicely together. Headlock doesn’t benefit you, but Grappler will get you\n\tAdvantage to hit your Grappled targets.\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-ability-score-increase",
      "heading": "Ability Score Increase",
      "sourceAnchor": "ability-score-increase",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-ability-score-increase-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Exactly the right abilities for this feat. Dexterity is there for Monks."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-headlock",
      "heading": "Headlock",
      "sourceAnchor": "headlock",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-headlock-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n\tFantastic if you’re not planning to bind your grappled target in\n\tchains/manacles/rope, which may not be worth the Action against weaker\n\tenemies. This doesn’t benefit you, unfortunately, but that’s what the Grappler\n\tfeat is for.\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-headlock-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n\tOf course, you can also shove enemies Prone if you want Advantage for your\n\tallies. It’s less optimizable than in the 2014 rules, unfortunately, and it\n\tdoes require an additional attack, so this may be faster for quickly\n\teliminating foes.\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-sturdy-knot",
      "heading": "Sturdy Knot",
      "sourceAnchor": "sturdy-knot",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-sturdy-knot-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n\tThe base DC’s to escape are 18 for chains, 20 for manacles, and 15 for rope.\n\tThe DCs to burst them are higher. Those DCs are decently high, but enemies\n\tstill have a chance to escape even with a negative Dexterity Modifier. Adding\n\tyour PB to the DCs will make it impossible for many enemies to escape.\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-sturdy-knot-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n\tUsing chains, manacles, and rope in combat is laughably easy in the 2024 DnD\n\trules. Your target must be Grappled, Incapacitated, or Restrained, then you\n\tuse a Utilize Action to bind them. A Monk can easily do this in one turn since\n\ttheir Martial Arts attack can be used to Grapple. Grab some chains and you’re\n\tnearly unstoppable.\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-tough-talk",
      "heading": "Tough Talk",
      "sourceAnchor": "tough-talk",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-tough-talk-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n\tA great reminder that the Attitude rules exist, but characters built for\n\tgrappling are very rarely good in social situations anyway.\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
